{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When Nathan the prophet came to him</b> — when Nathan prophesied concerning David and said to him: \"Also YHWH has removed your sin; you shall not die\" (II Samuel 12:13), for the word \"also\" teaches that he had already repented; therefore he said to him: \"has removed your sin.\" And I have already explained the matter of Bathsheba, that she was not in truth a married woman."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:30.225926842Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}